  "blocks": [
    {
      "object": "block",
      "id": "40fa6e41-f23e-805b-8d6c-eb854690502c",
      "parent": {
        "type": "page_id",
        "page_id": "40fa6e41-f23e-80e2-8635-fc3560ec38c9"
      },
      "created_time": "2026-11-05T07:36:00.000Z",
      "last_edited_time": "2026-11-05T08:05:00.000Z",
      "created_by": {
        "object": "user",
        "id": "00c350d3-9f7b-4bc1-b27d-24e15ac5139f"
      },
      "last_edited_by": {
        "object": "user",
        "id": "00c350d3-9f7b-4bc1-b27d-24e15ac5139f"
      },
      "has_children": false,
      "in_trash": false,
      "type": "paragraph",
      "paragraph": {
        "rich_text": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": {
              "content": "What’s the difference between “field building” and “community building”? I liked this definition that my wife came up with: a “field” is professional (eg “Technical AI Safety”), and building that is the act of eg causing more researchers to exist. Versus, a “community” is a specific group of people who bump into each other repeatedly.",
              "link": null
            },
            "annotations": {
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false,
              "strikethrough": false,
              "underline": false,
              "code": false,
              "color": "default"
            },
            "plain_text": "What’s the difference between “field building” and “community building”? I liked this definition that my wife came up with: a “field” is professional (eg “Technical AI Safety”), and building that is the act of eg causing more researchers to exist. Versus, a “community” is a specific group of people who bump into each other repeatedly.",
            "href": null
          }
        ],
        "icon": null,
        "color": "default"
      }
    },
    {
      "object": "block",
      "id": "40fa6e41-f23e-808b-a615-c94a0655a5ab",
      "parent": {
        "type": "page_id",
        "page_id": "40fa6e41-f23e-80e2-8635-fc3560ec38c9"
      },
      "created_time": "2026-11-05T07:40:00.000Z",
      "last_edited_time": "2026-11-05T07:58:00.000Z",
      "created_by": {
        "object": "user",
        "id": "00c350d3-9f7b-4bc1-b27d-24e15ac5139f"
      },
      "last_edited_by": {
        "object": "user",
        "id": "00c350d3-9f7b-4bc1-b27d-24e15ac5139f"
      },
      "has_children": false,
      "in_trash": false,
      "type": "paragraph",
      "paragraph": {
        "rich_text": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": {
              "content": "Field building might be more scaleable, impersonal, metrics-driven. Community building feels more cozy, bespoke, vibesy.",
              "link": null
            },
            "annotations": {
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false,
              "strikethrough": false,
              "underline": false,
              "code": false,
              "color": "default"
            },
            "plain_text": "Field building might be more scaleable, impersonal, metrics-driven. Community building feels more cozy, bespoke, vibesy.",
            "href": null
          }
        ],
        "icon": null,
        "color": "default"
      }
    },
    {
      "object": "block",
      "id": "40fa6e41-f23e-80f5-a741-d81b6ef7e994",
      "parent": {
        "type": "page_id",
        "page_id": "40fa6e41-f23e-80e2-8635-fc3560ec38c9"
      },
      "created_time": "2026-11-05T07:43:00.000Z",
      "last_edited_time": "2026-11-05T07:49:00.000Z",
      "created_by": {
        "object": "user",
        "id": "00c350d3-9f7b-4bc1-b27d-24e15ac5139f"
      },
      "last_edited_by": {
        "object": "user",
        "id": "00c350d3-9f7b-4bc1-b27d-24e15ac5139f"
      },
      "has_children": false,
      "in_trash": false,
      "type": "paragraph",
      "paragraph": {
        "rich_text": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": {
              "content": "With a definition like that, you might think I’m stacking the deck in favor of “community building” — doesn’t this frame presuppose that community is better?",
              "link": null
            },
            "annotations": {
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false,
              "strikethrough": false,
              "underline": false,
              "code": false,
              "color": "default"
            },
            "plain_text": "With a definition like that, you might think I’m stacking the deck in favor of “community building” — doesn’t this frame presuppose that community is better?",
            "href": null
          }
        ],
        "icon": null,
        "color": "default"
      }
    },
    {
      "object": "block",
      "id": "40fa6e41-f23e-80d0-8bf5-d5436c4a5fb3",
      "parent": {
        "type": "page_id",
        "page_id": "40fa6e41-f23e-80e2-8635-fc3560ec38c9"
      },
      "created_time": "2026-11-05T07:50:00.000Z",
      "last_edited_time": "2026-11-05T08:23:00.000Z",
      "created_by": {
        "object": "user",
        "id": "00c350d3-9f7b-4bc1-b27d-24e15ac5139f"
      },
      "last_edited_by": {
        "object": "user",
        "id": "00c350d3-9f7b-4bc1-b27d-24e15ac5139f"
      },
      "has_children": false,
      "in_trash": false,
      "type": "paragraph",
      "paragraph": {
        "rich_text": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": {
              "content": "(And, it’s definitely easier for me to reason about community building. Many of my projects lean into a cozy community vibe. Community sure seems to be in short supply in the modern era. People need friends more than they need jobs!)",
              "link": null
            },
            "annotations": {
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false,
              "strikethrough": false,
              "underline": false,
              "code": false,
              "color": "default"
            },
            "plain_text": "(And, it’s definitely easier for me to reason about community building. Many of my projects lean into a cozy community vibe. Community sure seems to be in short supply in the modern era. People need friends more than they need jobs!)",
            "href": null
          }
        ],
        "icon": null,
        "color": "default"
      }
    },
    {
      "object": "block",
      "id": "40fa6e41-f23e-807c-b7b3-fea5bc08a365",
      "parent": {
        "type": "page_id",
        "page_id": "40fa6e41-f23e-80e2-8635-fc3560ec38c9"
      },
      "created_time": "2026-11-05T07:44:00.000Z",
      "last_edited_time": "2026-11-05T08:32:00.000Z",
      "created_by": {
        "object": "user",
        "id": "00c350d3-9f7b-4bc1-b27d-24e15ac5139f"
      },
      "last_edited_by": {
        "object": "user",
        "id": "00c350d3-9f7b-4bc1-b27d-24e15ac5139f"
      },
      "has_children": false,
      "in_trash": false,
      "type": "paragraph",
      "paragraph": {
        "rich_text": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": {
              "content": "But there seem to be limits to how far you get with community building. I also care a lot about scaleability, and it seems like communities hit certain limits (famously, Dunbar’s number). One read of where Manifold went wrong is that it never figured out how to be a platform that served multiple communities (like subreddits), vs a single hivemind community that hit its carrying capacity.",
              "link": null
            },
            "annotations": {
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false,
              "strikethrough": false,
              "underline": false,
              "code": false,
              "color": "default"
            },
            "plain_text": "But there seem to be limits to how far you get with community building. I also care a lot about scaleability, and it seems like communities hit certain limits (famously, Dunbar’s number). One read of where Manifold went wrong is that it never figured out how to be a platform that served multiple communities (like subreddits), vs a single hivemind community that hit its carrying capacity.",
            "href": null
          }
        ],
        "icon": null,
        "color": "default"
      }
    },
    {
      "object": "block",
      "id": "40fa6e41-f23e-8027-a718-cec270fb23b8",
      "parent": {
        "type": "page_id",
        "page_id": "40fa6e41-f23e-80e2-8635-fc3560ec38c9"
      },
      "created_time": "2026-11-05T07:52:00.000Z",
      "last_edited_time": "2026-11-05T08:23:00.000Z",
      "created_by": {
        "object": "user",
        "id": "00c350d3-9f7b-4bc1-b27d-24e15ac5139f"
      },
      "last_edited_by": {
        "object": "user",
        "id": "00c350d3-9f7b-4bc1-b27d-24e15ac5139f"
      },
      "has_children": false,
      "in_trash": false,
      "type": "paragraph",
      "paragraph": {
        "rich_text": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": {
              "content": "Community building also runs into personal limitations — I can only keep track of so many different unique people in my fallible monkey brain. (These days, every time I get to know someone new, I feel like my brain must be evicting somebody else to make room…)",
              "link": null
            },
            "annotations": {
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false,
              "strikethrough": false,
              "underline": false,
              "code": false,
              "color": "default"
            },
            "plain_text": "Community building also runs into personal limitations — I can only keep track of so many different unique people in my fallible monkey brain. (These days, every time I get to know someone new, I feel like my brain must be evicting somebody else to make room…)",
            "href": null
          }
        ],
        "icon": null,
        "color": "default"
      }
    },
    {
      "object": "block",
      "id": "40fa6e41-f23e-8000-a6b9-d370b4f18a70",
      "parent": {
        "type": "page_id",
        "page_id": "40fa6e41-f23e-80e2-8635-fc3560ec38c9"
      },
      "created_time": "2026-11-05T08:17:00.000Z",
      "last_edited_time": "2026-11-05T08:17:00.000Z",
