    {
      "object": "block",
      "id": "40fa6e41-f23e-8025-91c2-cb560f90a8e0",
      "parent": {
        "type": "page_id",
        "page_id": "40fa6e41-f23e-80e2-8635-fc3560ec38c9"
      },
      "created_time": "2026-11-05T07:43:00.000Z",
      "last_edited_time": "2026-11-05T08:26:00.000Z",
      "created_by": {
        "object": "user",
        "id": "00c350d3-9f7b-4bc1-b27d-24e15ac5139f"
      },
      "last_edited_by": {
        "object": "user",
        "id": "00c350d3-9f7b-4bc1-b27d-24e15ac5139f"
      },
      "has_children": false,
      "in_trash": false,
      "type": "paragraph",
      "paragraph": {
        "rich_text": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": {
              "content": "I think AI safety and EA have historically been “communities”, and now find themselves needing or wanting to become “fields”. A bunch of old-school intuitions may not apply — it’s no longer a few hundred people going to each other’s parties.",
              "link": null
            },
            "annotations": {
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false,
              "strikethrough": false,
              "underline": false,
              "code": false,
              "color": "default"
            },
            "plain_text": "I think AI safety and EA have historically been “communities”, and now find themselves needing or wanting to become “fields”. A bunch of old-school intuitions may not apply — it’s no longer a few hundred people going to each other’s parties.",
            "href": null
          }
        ],
        "icon": null,
        "color": "default"
      }
    },
    {
      "object": "block",
      "id": "40fa6e41-f23e-8046-93b1-fd38ed8336b8",
      "parent": {
        "type": "page_id",
        "page_id": "40fa6e41-f23e-80e2-8635-fc3560ec38c9"
      },
      "created_time": "2026-11-05T07:42:00.000Z",
      "last_edited_time": "2026-11-05T08:22:00.000Z",
      "created_by": {
        "object": "user",
        "id": "00c350d3-9f7b-4bc1-b27d-24e15ac5139f"
      },
      "last_edited_by": {
        "object": "user",
        "id": "00c350d3-9f7b-4bc1-b27d-24e15ac5139f"
      },
      "has_children": false,
      "in_trash": false,
      "type": "paragraph",
      "paragraph": {
        "rich_text": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": {
              "content": "Perhaps, one way to scale up a field is by creating more and more distinct communities within it. A subfield might be small enough to be its own community.",
              "link": null
            },
            "annotations": {
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false,
              "strikethrough": false,
              "underline": false,
              "code": false,
              "color": "default"
            },
            "plain_text": "Perhaps, one way to scale up a field is by creating more and more distinct communities within it. A subfield might be small enough to be its own community.",
            "href": null
          }
        ],
        "icon": null,
        "color": "default"
      }
    },
